t pick up on that  how about you guys for any of you out  there who read the harry potter books  before you saw the movies did you  suspect  snape all along or did you see the  quarrel twist coming i'd love to hear  your thoughts down in the comments  number two is the acting and to be  completely fair here this one was  largely unavoidable with the movie  needing so many young and in some cases  inexperienced actors to play prominent  roles  we all know dan radcliffe emma watson  and rupert grint would grow into their  roles over time but there were some  rocky moments in the early going  to wb's credit they balanced out the  child actors by pairing them with an  absolutely stellar lineup of adult cast  members  maggie smith alan rickman richard harris  and robbie coltrane play their roles to  perfection  not to mention those in minor roles like  john hurd as ollivander richard  griffiths as uncle vernon and warwick  davis as professor flitwick  number three no potions challenge while  the first couple movies stayed more true  to the books than the others that would  follow one key scene they missed out on  was the potions challenge near the  climax of the story  before harry can get to the final room  where quirrell is waiting for him with  the mirror of era said  he and hermione must solve what is  essentially a logic puzzle involving  potions  unfortunately this scene was absent from  the film harry got a chance to stand out  with the winged keys and ron proved his  value to the trio with the wizards chess  challenge  the writers probably felt her mindy  stand out moment then would be taken  care of by her quick thinking to escape  the devil's snare  except that's actually not how it  happens in the book in the books it's  actually hermione who panics when the  trio finds themselves within the devil  snare  ron remains calm and helps to calm her  down long enough so she can escape  before the plant has a firm grip  she then frees both harry and ron with  bluebell flames  now keeping this closer to the book  version would have actually given both  ron  and hermione a bit of a standout moment  there in the devil snare trial and then  they could have still went on to give  hermione  another amazing moment had they included  the potions challenge  we know she's smart and we know she's  brave and the potions challenge to me  is just the perfect moment to show both  of those things  and as we all know hermione would go on  to bail out harry and ron numerous times  throughout the rest of the series  thanks to that knowledge and bravery  number 4 the quirrell voldemort timeline  harry and quirrell meet for the first  time in the leaky cauldron before the  start of term at hogwarts  in the movie squirrel already has his  turban and doesn't shake harry's hand  when offered  this would seem to imply that quirrell  knew he couldn't touch harry  and yet at the end of the movie he  appears confused after touching harry  only to find his hand as burned  this took place differently in the books  and would help to make both scenes make  more sense  in the book version quirrell and harry  still meet in the leaky cauldron however  quirrell  doesn't yet have his turban he actually  goes on to shake harry's hand in the  books as well  quirrell actually doesn't start wearing  the turban in the books until after the  attempted break-in at gringotts which we  know took place  the very same day that he and harry met  this also means that when harry  originally met quirrell in the leaky  cauldron  voldemort had not yet possessed him this  may seem like a minor detail however it  would certainly have made quarrels shock  in the final scene  make more sense had they followed the  book timeline a little more closely  number five no peeves the poltergeist  how could the movies leave out peeves  yes he's a minor character but longtime  fans know  just how much comic relief peeves  provides throughout the series  he wouldn't have even needed to be  featured prominently to make an impact  he's one of those characters who can  make just  random off-the-cuff comments and still  serve his purpose  as a result of peeves not being in we  lose out on the scene where harry  impersonates the bloody baron while he's  hiding under the invisibility cloak  which is  a scene i just loved from the books now  believe it or not peeves was  actually cast and even filmed some  scenes for sorcerer's stone before  director chris columbus ultimately  decided to cut the part  apparently columbus ended up not being  satisfied with the final look for peeves  and that's why he said  getting rid of it at least that's what  the most common story is  who knows what really happened i  personally love re-watching the movies  for the nostalgia and being such a fan  of the world i can appreciate them even  without a strong plot to propel that  viewing experience forward  if you've never seen the movies before  they're certainly worth watching at  least once  and for long time fans they'll be  something you want to revisit again and  again as the years go by even if they do  have their share of flaws as always guys  and gals thank you so much for watching  i'll talk to you again soon
 

